 In *Process and Reality*, Whitehead described the cosmos as a process of becoming, composed of actual occasions that prehend their predecessors and synthesize them into novel unities. The past is not dead. It is actively taken up into every present moment. Bergson's *élan vital* — the vital impulse that drives creative evolution — is not a mystical force. It is the continuous creation of novelty, and morphic resonance is the canal that directs it without fixing it. The field does not determine the form. It constrains the possibility space, making some forms probable and others so improbable that they require a rupture to emerge.
 
